<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#associates-of-the-swiss-confederacy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Associates of the Swiss Confederacy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zugewandte Orte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Associates of the Swiss Confederacy, in German zugewandte Orte, were territories allied to the Old Swiss Confederacy without being full member cantons. They included the Abbey and City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>, the Three Leagues of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, Biel and Mulhouse. Bound to the Confederates by treaties of protection and alliance, they had a lesser standing at the Diet, and several became cantons in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/associates-of-the-swiss-confederacy.jpg" alt="Associates of the Swiss Confederacy" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 19:13, 3 May 2007 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Zugewandte_Orte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
